id: pm-memory-x47g
title: Pool-lane stop test assumes the failing batch wins the first worker slot
description: "test/worker-budget.test.ts 'one failed batch stops every pool lane from claiming further batches' failed on pm-memory#47 (release gate (26, npm), run 41858914984): '12 of 12 batches started after the first failure'. The assertion assumes batch 0, the failing one, runs before the other lanes drain the list. Nothing guarantees that: worker slots are shared by every test file under the same node --test parent (memory-worker-slots-<ppid>) and are won by 25 ms polling, not in claim order. While the property suites hold slots, lane 0 can keep losing the poll while lanes 1-3 run batches 1-11, so all 12 start and the assertion fails although the pool behaves as designed. #47 changes only tracker files, so the failure is independent of its diff."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,flaky,test
created_at: "2026-11-04T16:51:21.953Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T17:13:32.194Z"
assignee: claude-hub
claim_principal: claude-hub
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "The lane-stop property is tested deterministically, independent of worker-slot scheduling and runner load: after one batch fails no lane claims another, and lanes already running finish their batch; the real-process pool test keeps checking rejection and cleanup; runModelWorkerPool behaviour is unchanged."
severity: medium
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T16:53:07.565Z",claude-hub,"Fix: the lane loop moves out of runModelWorkerPool into an exported poolLanes(width, count, run) with identical semantics. A new test drives poolLanes with controlled promises: batch 0 fails only once all four lanes are busy, and batches 1-3 finish only after that failure is recorded. Exactly batches 0-3 must start, and the pool must return the one failure. It also checks that without a failure every batch runs once and that a pool never runs wider than its list. The real-process pool test keeps its rejection and cleanup assertions and drops the slot-order-dependent count. Revert check: removing the failures.length === 0 guard from the lane loop fails the new test. worker-budget passes 7/7 under Node and Bun; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication and identity:check pass."
  "2026-11-04T16:53:26.781Z",claude-hub,"Fix: the lane loop moves out of runModelWorkerPool into an exported poolLanes(width, count, run) with identical semantics. A new test drives poolLanes with controlled promises: batch 0 fails only once all four lanes are busy, and batches 1-3 finish only after that failure is recorded. Exactly batches 0-3 must start, and the pool must return the one failure. It also checks that without a failure every batch runs once and that a pool never runs wider than its list. The real-process pool test keeps its rejection and cleanup assertions and drops the slot-order-dependent count. Revert check: removing the failures.length === 0 guard from the lane loop fails the new test. worker-budget passes 7/7 under Node and Bun; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication and identity:check pass."
  "2026-11-04T17:13:32.194Z",claude-hub,"Review round 1 on 68e888e, both findings fixed. (1) CodeRabbit: the stop test recorded starts but not completions, so a pool returning while batches 1-3 still ran would pass. It now asserts that batches 1-3 finished before poolLanes resolved, and replacing Promise.all with Promise.race fails it. (2) Sourcery: a non-Error rejection went into the Error[] through a cast. poolLanes now wraps it in an Error naming the batch, with the original value as cause, and the test covers it. worker-budget passes 7/7 under Node and Bun; typecheck and lint pass."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  test/helpers.ts,project
  test/worker-budget.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test test/worker-budget.test.ts,project,claude-hub,"2026-11-04T16:53:06.049Z",local_mutation,fix/pool-stop-test-independent-of-slot-order
